WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.825
Two thousand years ago,

00:00:01.825 --> 00:00:05.238
the founding text of
Chinese medicine opens

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:06.190
on a boast —

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:10.000
and the emperor himself is
the one who makes it.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.012
I have heard that the
people of high antiquity all

00:00:13.012 --> 00:00:14.639
lived past a hundred years,

00:00:14.639 --> 00:00:16.807
and their movements never
weakened —

00:00:16.807 --> 00:00:19.819
that the years did not wear
them down as they wear

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:20.000
us.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:30.000
It's false. Not exaggerated
— false.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:30.850
They did not.

00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:33.922
The people who wrote that
sentence died younger

00:00:33.922 --> 00:00:36.405
than the ancestors they
were praising.

00:00:36.405 --> 00:00:39.020
The golden age was
already a memory that

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:40.000
never happened.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.151
Then I have opened my
own canon with a rumour.

00:00:43.151 --> 00:00:46.575
The first line of the book
my physicians swear by,

00:00:46.575 --> 00:00:50.000
and it is only something
that somebody once heard.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.922
It is not lying to you. It is
persuading you.

00:00:52.922 --> 00:00:54.870
Those are not the same
thing —

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:57.792
and the physician's
answer is narrower still:

00:00:57.792 --> 00:01:00.000
those among them who
knew the Way.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.113
So why did an entire
civilisation copy that one

00:01:03.113 --> 00:01:06.093
sentence, faithfully, for
two thousand years?

00:01:06.093 --> 00:01:08.742
The Emperor's Inner
Canon. Chapter One —

00:01:08.742 --> 00:01:10.000
The First Sentence.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:16.753
A dramatized adaptation of
a classical philosophical

00:01:16.753 --> 00:01:20.000
text. Not medical advice.
